        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(heartbeat): inject Slack interaction value into heartbeat prompt\\…",
        "body": "Fixes #99544\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes #99544 (follow-up to #61502). Slack interactive button clicks wake the target session and thread, but the clicked action's `value` / `action_id` never reaches the agent as input. `consumeSelectedSystemEventEntries` removes the interaction entry from the system event queue, yet the event text was never injected into the heartbeat prompt.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nThe heartbeat runner's prompt resolution has dedicated builders for exec-completion and cron events, but the generic fallback path never includes system event text. When a Slack hook wake triggers a heartbeat with no exec/cron events, the generic heartbeat prompt is used and the interaction payload is silently dropped.\r\n\r\nThis change adds a Slack-interaction-typed branch:\r\n\r\n- `src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.ts`: add `isSlackInteractionEvent()` and `buildSlackInteractionEventPrompt()`\r\n- `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts`: route pending system events whose `contextKey` starts with `slack:interaction:` to the new builder, mirroring the exec/cron branches\r\n\r\nUnlike a generic \"prepend all system event text\" approach, this only touches events explicitly queued as Slack interactions, so it does not widen the prompt-injection surface for arbitrary system events.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers clicking Slack interactive buttons will see the `action_id` and `value` reflected in the agent's heartbeat turn, allowing workflows that depend on button clicks to act on the selected verb. No other heartbeat behavior changes.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nUnit tests:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.test.ts\r\n\r\n ✓ |unit-fast| src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.test.ts (51 tests) 13ms\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  51 passed (51)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIntegration test:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/infra/heartbeat-runner.slack-interaction.test.ts\r\n\r\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/heartbeat-runner.slack-interaction.test.ts (1 test) 49ms\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nRegression check on existing heartbeat runner tests:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/infra/heartbeat-runner.returns-default-unset.test.ts\r\n\r\n ✓ |infra| src/infra/heartbeat-runner.returns-default-unset.test.ts (43 tests) 524ms\r\n\r\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\r\n      Tests  43 passed (43)\r\n```\r\n\r\nFormat / lint:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.test.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.slack-interaction.test.ts\r\nAll matched files use the correct format.\r\n\r\n$ npx oxlint@latest src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-events-filter.test.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts \\\r\n  src/infra/heartbeat-runner.slack-interaction.test.ts\r\nFound 0 warnings and 0 errors.\r\n\r\n$ git diff --check\r\n# no output\r\n```\r\n\r\nKey assertions from the integration test show the prompt body contains:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSlack interactive button was clicked: action_id=\"approve_pr\" with value=\"merge-99544\". Please act on this interaction.\r\n```\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/99544-slack-interaction-heartbeat-prompt",
